## CBI site profile for R
##
## Prefer cairo for bitmap devices when X11 is unavailable.
##
## R decides options(bitmapType) at startup and picks "Xlib" unless its
## stricter cairo check passes.  On a build configured with --with-x=no there
## is no X11, so png()/jpeg()/tiff() without an explicit type= cannot work,
## even under xvfb-run.  cairo is built in and does work, so prefer it.
##
## This belongs in the site profile rather than in the user's session because
## options() do not cross process boundaries: R CMD INSTALL runs the package
## lazy-load step in a subprocess, and packages that open a device while being
## loaded (e.g. inventorize) fail there regardless of what the calling session
## set.  The site profile is read by those subprocesses.
##
## The test is made at run time so this file is safe on builds that do have
## X11, where "Xlib" remains the default.
if (!capabilities("X11") && capabilities("cairo")) {
    options(bitmapType = "cairo")
}
